"epic hidden note" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-hidden-note&gt;
		<header>The &lt;epic-hidden-note&gt; element: the line under a filtered list, 3 hidden · show all.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph><text code>&lt;epic-hidden-note&gt;</> is the quiet line under a list the state filter hides items of: "3 hidden · show all". A click shows them all again.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>For anyone changing how items are filtered.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Status: <label size="mini" color="green">built</> (epic <text code>epic-engine</> P3), in the <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-state-filter" link="/epic/src/components/epic-state-filter/"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-state-filter/" code>epic-state-filter</></> family, with <link target="src-spell-epic-src-docs-epic-state-filter-html" link="/epic-state-filter"><text code>&lt;epic-state-filter&gt;</></>.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its vocabulary: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-state-filter-epichiddennote-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-state-filter/EpicHiddenNote.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-state-filter/EpicHiddenNote.en.ts" code>EpicHiddenNote.en.ts</></></>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its component: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-state-filter-epichiddennote-tsx" link="/epic/src/components/epic-state-filter/EpicHiddenNote.tsx"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-state-filter/EpicHiddenNote.tsx" code>EpicHiddenNote.tsx</></>.</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<example "Example">
			<html>
				<epic-hidden-note count="3"></epic-hidden-note>
			</html>
		</example>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>Nobody writes it in a doc: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-docs-epic-section-html" link="/epic-section"><text code>&lt;epic-section&gt;</></> draws it under its items, and the docs runtime under each of the Epics page's lists (<link target="src-spell-epic-src-tools-assets-spell-doc-runtime-js" link="/epic/src/tools/_assets/spell-doc-runtime.js"><text title="epic/src/tools/_assets/spell-doc-runtime.js" code>wireItemFilters()</></>). With nothing hidden, its owner leaves it out.</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Where it goes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="compass"/>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Parent</>
				<cell>How many</>
				<cell>As</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell><text code>&lt;epic-section&gt;</>, under its items</>
				<cell>one</>
				<cell>Its part <text code>hidden-note</>.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>a docs page, after a filtered list</>
				<cell>one per list</>
				<cell><text code>.spell-hidden-note</>.</>
			</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>It has no children.</>
	</>

	<section label="4. Attributes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="table columns"/>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Attribute</>
				<cell>What it is</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>count</>
				</>
				<cell>How many items the filter hides.</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Parts" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>Pieces of what it draws.</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
